@startuml
title Admin Views Reservations
autonumber
actor Admin
participant "Postman / API Client" as Client
participant "Massage Reservation API" as API
participant "Authentication Middleware" as Auth
participant "Reservation Controller" as Controller
database MongoDB as DB

Admin -> Client: Request all reservations
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/reservations\n(Admin Bearer token)
API -> Auth: Verify token and load user
Auth -> DB: Find user and check token version
DB --> Auth: Admin account
alt Token is valid
    Auth --> API: Authenticated admin
    API -> Controller: getMyReservations
    Controller -> Controller: Check user's admin role
    Controller -> DB: Find all reservations
    DB --> Controller: Reservation list
    Controller --> API: 200 OK
    API --> Client: All reservations
    Client --> Admin: Display reservations
else Token is invalid or expired
    Auth --> API: 401 Unauthorized
    API --> Client: Error response
    Client --> Admin: Show error
end
note over Controller
    A non-admin receives only their own reservations.
    Admins can also retrieve a specific reservation by id.
end note
@enduml
